    "highlights": [
      "New York's price level is the 5th highest of 51 states and DC, so labor, permits and extras cost more here than almost anywhere: about $701 of labor on a gas tank against $650 nationally.",
      "Electricity is expensive in New York (26.39 cents per kWh, the 7th highest), so a standard electric tank costs about $947 a year to run and a heat pump saves about $715 a year against it.",
      "Incoming water drops to about 42.0 °F in the coldest month, so a whole-house tankless unit manages only one full-flow shower at a time in winter; a tank, or two tankless units, suits larger households better.",
      "11% of New York homes still heat water with fuel oil, often from the heating boiler; those systems are priced differently from the tanks on this page.",
      "Where you live inside New York matters: the same 50-gallon gas job is about $1,924 in the New York-Newark-Jersey City, NY-NJ area and $1,770 in the Syracuse, NY area."
    ]
